# Conventional Commits

All commit messages MUST follow Conventional Commits.

## Format

```text
type(optional-scope): subject

optional body

optional footer
```

## Types (English)

Use one of: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`.

## Scope

- English, kebab or short noun
- Recommended: `txfio`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `docs`
- Other scopes are allowed; not a closed whitelist

## Subject

- Japanese is allowed (and preferred when it communicates intent better)
- Type and scope stay in English
- Imperative / concise; no trailing period required

## Breaking changes

Use `type(scope)!: subject` and/or a footer:

```text
BREAKING CHANGE: description
```

## Examples

```text
feat(txfio): コミット時の rename 適用を追加
docs: 設計ドキュメントを docs/design.md へ移す
chore(repo): リポジトリ基盤を追加
```

## Agent behavior

When creating commits in this repository, draft messages in this format. Do not use free-form subjects without a type prefix.
